  "title": "Strong Optimality of Two-Color Permutation Wordle at n=3",
  "batch_label": "49",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For the exact two-color Permutation Wordle game at n=3 frozen in source.md and interpreted in problem.md, the optimal deterministic success counts are (N_1,N_2,N_3,N_4,N_5,N_6)=(1,8,24,40,47,48), and N_r=48 for every r>=6. The Kutin--Smithline multicolor CircularShift algorithm, read by its circuit-completion prose, Figure 6, and the proof of Lemma 4.4 in arXiv:2408.00903v3, has exact-round counts (1,7,16,16,7,1) and therefore attains N_r simultaneously for every r>=1. The displayed color-update cases in Definition 4.3 conflict with those parts of the primary source; this claim uses the exact operational interpretation documented in evidence/circular-shift-interpretation.md and does not assert that the inconsistent displayed cases literally produce the same strategy.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
